<title>PORTUGAL: SOCCER SHOWCASE-FACTS AND FIGURES FOR BENFICA V PORTO.</title>
<headline>SOCCER SHOWCASE-FACTS AND FIGURES FOR BENFICA V PORTO.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Facts and figures for Saturday's</p>
<p>Portuguese first division match between Benfica and Porto.</p>
<p>BENFICA:</p>
<p>Founded in 1904 as Sport Lisboa. Sport Lisboa &amp; Benfica</p>
<p>since 1908.</p>
<p>Major honours: European Cup winners: 1961, 1962</p>
<p>Portuguese league champions (30): 1936, 1937, 1938,</p>
<p>1942,1943, 1945, 1950, 1955, 1957, 1960, 1961, 1963, 1964, 1965,</p>
<p>1967, 1968, 1969, 1971, 1972, 1973, 1975, 1976, 1977, 1981,</p>
<p>1983, 1984, 1987, 1989, 1991, 1994.</p>
<p>Portuguese Cup winners (23): 1940, 1943, 1944, 1949, 1951,</p>
<p>1952, 1953, 1955, 1957, 1959, 1962, 1964, 1969, 1970, 1972,1980,</p>
<p>1981, 1983, 1985, 1986, 1987, 1993, 1996.</p>
<p>Supercup winners (3): 1980, 1985, 1989</p>
<p>Ground. Estadio da Luz (Stadium of Light). capacity: 115,000</p>
<p>Manager/trainer: Paulo Autuori (Brazil), since June 1996</p>
<p>Record league appearances: Tamagnini Nene 421</p>
<p>Record league goalscorer: Eusebio Ferreira 317</p>
<p>Most capped player: Tamagnini Nene 66</p>
<p>Final league position last season: 3rd</p>
<p>Record league win at home: 13-1 against Sanjoanense (1947)</p>
<p>Record defeat at home: 1-4 against Sporting (1948)</p>
<p>Record victory away: 9-0 against Beira-Mar (1967)</p>
<p>Record defeat away: 1-7 against Sporting (1987)</p>
<p>Home kit: shirts red, shorts white</p>
<p>Nickname: &quot;eagles&quot;</p>
<p>PORTO:</p>
<p>Founded in 1906.</p>
<p>Major honours: European Cup winners in 1987</p>
<p>			 Intercontinental Cup winner in 1987</p>
<p>			 European Super Cup 1988</p>
<p>League champions (15): 1935, 1939, 1940, 1956, 1959, 1978,</p>
<p>1979, 1985, 1986, 1988, 1990, 1992, 1993, 1995, 1996.</p>
<p>Portuguese Cup winners (8): 1956, 1958, 1968, 1977, 1984,</p>
<p>1988, 1991, 1994.</p>
<p>Supercup winners (9): 1981, 1983, 1984, 1986, 1990, 1991,</p>
<p>1993, 1994, 1996.</p>
<p>Ground: Estadio das Antas, capacity 76,000.</p>
<p>Manager/trainer: Antonio Oliveira), since June 1996</p>
<p>Record league appearances: Joao Pinto 398</p>
<p>Record league goalscorer: Fernando Gomes 288</p>
<p>Most capped player: Joao Pinto 70</p>
<p>Final league position last season: 1st</p>
<p>Record victory at home: 12-1 against Carcavelinhos (1942)</p>
<p>Record defeat at home: 2-6 against Belenenses (1945)</p>
<p>Record victory away: 12-1 against Academico (1939)</p>
<p>Record defeat away: 2-12 against Benfica (1943)</p>
<p>Home kit: shirts blue/white, shorts blue</p>
<p>Nickname: &quot;dragons&quot;</p>
<p>The biggest scoreline between the two teams in the league</p>
<p>was Benfica's 12-2 home win in 1943.</p>
<p>Last September, Porto crushed Benfica 5-0 to win the</p>
<p>Supercup, the biggest ever Benfica defeat at the Stadium of</p>
<p>Light. Previously, the heaviest defeat had been 5-1 against</p>
<p>Manchester United in a European Cup match in 1966.</p>
<p>Benfica-Porto last 10 seasons league results:</p>
<p>Benfica's ground - 3-1, 1-1, 0-0, 0-0, 2-2, 2-3, 0-0, 2-0,</p>
<p>1-1, 2-1.</p>
<p>Porto's ground - 2-2, 0-3, 0-0, 0-1, 0-2, 0-0, 1-0, 3-3,</p>
<p>2-1, 3-0.</p>
</text>
